	url = {https://doi.org/10.1145/3369199.3369206},
	doi = {10.1145/3369199.3369206},
	abstract = {Symbolic learning theory is a very important topic in the current information explosion era. The 21st century is an era of "image civilization", which is characterized by the popularity of images and penetrate deeply all aspects of life. A large number of images appear in human life through the digital network, and unconsciously humans receive many image symbols. However, symbols recognition in images is an important key. The paper through the method of image reorganization, Exploring the influence of image symbols on human cognition by using the cultural products born from traditional Japanese aesthetics. Using Saussure's (1857-1913) Semiology to illustrate image cognition, and through the questionnaire survey method, for people's past experience in aesthetics and the relationship between cultural history and image cognition, and this paper look forward to providing a reference method of learning and teaching of symbols for future.},
